  "question": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0102_7440f886e025.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 185px;\" /></p><p>The figure shows a circular area of tthe radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> where a uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is going into the plane of the paper and increasing in magnitude at a constant rate. In that case, which of the following graphs, drawn schematically, correctly shows the variation of the induced electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></math>?</p>"
  },
